[I] Multilingual text processing library for input, display and editing

[T] The m17n library provides applications with a standard interface to handle
[T] multilingual text as an M-text object, including input method handling,
[T] complex text layout and multilingual text display/editing. It uses the
[T] language and script data supplied by the companion m17n-db package.

[U] https://www.nongnu.org/m17n/

[A] National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST)
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base

[L] LGPL
